{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"5ec73436d976815d","name":"card_event_on_the_ascend","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/WinterWar/events/card_event_on_the_ascend","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"ON THE ASCENT","text":"Destroy and Salvage the unit(s) with the least attack on the battlefield.","flavorText":"During the Second Sino-Japanese War, Japan significantly expanded its territorial control. The conflict, which began in 1937 and lasted until 1945, provided Japan with the opportunity to extend its territory across various regions in China. Within the first two years of the war, Japanese forces achieved rapid success, gaining control of most ports and major cities up to Hankow, and a large portion of the railway network. The expansion continued as Japanese forces moved further inland and took control of key areas such as Shansi, Inner Mongolia, and Canton. With control over key railways and the seas, along with superior air power which led to the destruction of the Chinese air force and widespread bombings of cities, the human cost for the Chinese was extremely high. Yet the Chinese forces did not yield and conquering all of China proved to be a much more difficult task than initially anticipated for the Japanese. This war eventually became part of the larger Pacific War, and Japan's focus shifted as the conflict expanded. Finally, the Second Sino-Japanese War ended with Japan's defeat in 1945.","faction":"Japan","type":"order","rarity":"Unique","cost":3,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_on_the_ascend","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_on_the_ascend_title","SourceString":"ON THE ASCENT","LocalizedString":"ON THE ASCENT"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_on_the_ascend_text","SourceString":"Destroy and Salvage the unit(s) with the least attack on the battlefield.","LocalizedString":"Destroy and Salvage the unit(s) with the least attack on the battlefield."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_on_the_ascend_history","SourceString":"During the Second Sino-Japanese War, Japan significantly expanded its territorial control. The conflict, which began in 1937 and lasted until 1945, provided Japan with the opportunity to extend its territory across various regions in China. Within the first two years of the war, Japanese forces achieved rapid success, gaining control of most ports and major cities up to Hankow, and a large portion of the railway network. The expansion continued as Japanese forces moved further inland and took control of key areas such as Shansi, Inner Mongolia, and Canton. With control over key railways and the seas, along with superior air power which led to the destruction of the Chinese air force and widespread bombings of cities, the human cost for the Chinese was extremely high. Yet the Chinese forces did not yield and conquering all of China proved to be a much more difficult task than initially anticipated for the Japanese. This war eventually became part of the larger Pacific War, and Japan's focus shifted as the conflict expanded. Finally, the Second Sino-Japanese War ended with Japan's defeat in 1945.","LocalizedString":"During the Second Sino-Japanese War, Japan significantly expanded its territorial control. The conflict, which began in 1937 and lasted until 1945, provided Japan with the opportunity to extend its territory across various regions in China. Within the first two years of the war, Japanese forces achieved rapid success, gaining control of most ports and major cities up to Hankow, and a large portion of the railway network. The expansion continued as Japanese forces moved further inland and took control of key areas such as Shansi, Inner Mongolia, and Canton. With control over key railways and the seas, along with superior air power which led to the destruction of the Chinese air force and widespread bombings of cities, the human cost for the Chinese was extremely high. Yet the Chinese forces did not yield and conquering all of China proved to be a much more difficult task than initially anticipated for the Japanese. This war eventually became part of the larger Pacific War, and Japan's focus shifted as the conflict expanded. Finally, the Second Sino-Japanese War ended with Japan's defeat in 1945."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WinterWar","isReserved":true,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_2'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_2.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Japan/CandidateArtwork/Winter_war/t_japanese_order_ww.t_japanese_order_ww","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Japanese WW2 poster","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/ON_THE_ASCENT.ON_THE_ASCENT","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":384.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_on_the_ascend_photo","SourceString":"Japanese infantry advancing in Beijing, China, 1937.","LocalizedString":"Japanese infantry advancing in Beijing, China, 1937."},"isDraw":true,"isDefenseBuff":true},"variables":[{"name":"attackValue","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"affectedUnits","type":"TArray<int32>","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"ExecuteUbergraph_card_event_on_the_ascend","owner":"card_event_on_the_ascend_C","params":[{"name":"EntryPoint","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"pure":false,"event":false,"flags":"FUNC_Final | FUNC_UbergraphFunction | FUNC_HasDefaults","locals":[{"name":"Temp_int_Array_Index_Variable","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"Temp_int_Loop_Counter_Variable","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Add_IntInt_ReturnValue","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"K2Node_Event_targetCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","directio